    private void toolHelp(){String help=kind.equals("lan")?"Choose a connected Wi-Fi, cellular, Ethernet or VPN subnet first. Auto uses its actual IPv4 subnet; CIDR, Range and Host preserve your manual targets. Android routing is the default and follows VPN rules. Tool options can explicitly bind a selected network; Android or VPN policy can deny that request. Use selected subnet copies the suggestion only when tapped. VPN /32 addresses do not reveal peers: enter a tailnet peer IP or subnet-router network manually. Interface-only entries are visible but cannot be bound. Android or VPN policies may block physical network access. Cellular addresses and reachability depend on Android and the carrier. Scans support up to 4,096 addresses. Sleeping devices and firewalls may hide hosts.":kind.equals("wifi")?"Android requires location permission and system Location for Wi-Fi scans. Scan throttling may return cached results; result details show age. Channel graphs estimate overlap, not actual RF utilization.":kind.equals("dns")?"Selected network DNS queries the resolver supplied by the chosen outgoing network. With System default routing, it uses the active network DNS. If the chosen network exposes no DNS, choose Custom resolver and enter an IP; a different network resolver is never substituted automatically. Custom resolver text is preserved when switching sources. DNS requests use the selected outgoing network and are sent directly without encryption.":kind.equals("trace")?"Uses hop-limited ICMP. Android support varies. Missing hops do not prove a routing failure.":kind.equals("speed")?"Real HTTPS transfer tests measure the internet path to the selected server. Transfer size applies separately to download and upload; protocol overhead is additional.":"Runs without root. Select Outgoing network to direct supported tools through Wi-Fi, cellular or VPN. Selected-network ping uses TCP reachability because Android system ping cannot bind to a Network handle. Tap any result row for full details and actions. Jobs stop when the app enters the background. Results and options are stored locally.";new AlertDialog.Builder(this).setTitle(name(kind)).setMessage(help).setPositiveButton("OK",null).show();}
